  GREEN P2SITE    FINDING  ONE selection is consumed at >=3 distinct (site-kind / movability) classes, and at least one PREDICATE over it does not move while the figures over it do — so "does the selection move" is underdetermined by the selection alone
        detail: classes=4 immovable-predicate=true
  GREEN P3SAT     FINDING  F2's verdict is stable TRUE across an interval in which the figure it is derived from moved — a saturated threshold over a movable selection. Registered asymmetry: a stable verdict is evidence only BECAUSE the figure is measured to move; it is uninterpretable otherwise
